{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The Shabbat burnt-offering on its Shabbat.</b> No ושעיר לכפר is said of it — to teach you that on festivals and on new moons, their sacrifices include a חטאת or an atonement-offering, and they come for atonement, therefore they established that they should read them and Israel go up for its reading as though they had offered them, as our Rabbis of blessed memory taught: as long as they read them, I account it to them as though they had offered them before Me. But the additional offering of Shabbat — neither חטאת nor כפרה is written of it — to teach you that its offerings do not come for atonement, because Shabbat itself atones; rather they come as a pleasing fragrance. Therefore one does not read the additional offering of Shabbat in the Torah like the others." "<b>And its libation.</b> It refers to the wine libations and the meal-offering libations of the daily burnt-offering. [Upon the daily burnt-offering, together with the daily burnt-offering.]"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:06.704528071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}